# ── This file is staged for the migration ──
# It sits inside WIP/ and its paths are written *relative to WIP/*, which means
# two things at once: it is already in force today (git reads a .gitignore in
# any directory, relative to that directory), and it is already correct on the
# day WIP/ becomes the repository root. Nothing has to be rewritten — the same
# trick as .github/workflows/ beside it. See MIGRATION.md.
#
# The root .gitignore currently carries these same rules with a `WIP/` prefix.
# Until the move they are duplicates, which is harmless; after it, the root one
# goes and this is the only copy.

# ── Output of generate_pages.py ──
# ~250 files: one index.html per post, member, publication and section, plus a
# redirect stub for every old-site URL. They are built in CI from the manifests
# and the index.html shell, so committing them would churn 250 files on every
# content edit and bury the one-line change that actually happened.
#
# index.html is NOT ignored — it is the template these are generated from. Nor
# is 404.html, which is hand-written.
news/*/index.html
news/index.html
people/*/index.html
people/index.html
publications/*/index.html
publications/index.html
research/index.html
research/*/index.html
information/
join/
services/
post/
publication/
authors/
jobs/

# sitemap.xml and llms.txt are generated by the same script and are ignored for
# the same reason, which is worth spelling out because the instinct is to keep
# them: **the committed copies are never the ones served.** CI runs
# generate_pages.py before uploading, so both are overwritten on every deploy.
# Committing them bought nothing and cost 51 KB of diff on every content edit —
# which is the same churn the ~250 pages above are ignored to avoid, just
# concentrated into two files. Run the generator to see them.
sitemap.xml
llms.txt

# ── Full-size sources for the derivatives ──
# Every one of these is the original a committed web copy was encoded from —
# keep them locally so a derivative can be regenerated, but they are megabytes
# each and no page ever requests them. See "The size budget" in CLAUDE.md.
*_full.jpg
*_full.png
img/Intro.mp4

# ── Local noise ──
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
*.DS_Store
